# Configuration contract for this project.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values. `.env` is gitignored;
# this file is committed on purpose, with keys but never with values, so the
# required configuration is discoverable without exposing any secret.
#
# None of these may be prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ — that prefix inlines the value
# into the JavaScript bundle sent to the browser, which would publish it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database — Neon PostgreSQL (TECH_STACK 2.13)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Do not fill these by hand. Run `neon env pull`, which writes them straight
# from Neon into .env — the credential never passes through a clipboard,
# a terminal, or a chat.
#
# Pooled connection, used by the application at runtime. A pooler reuses a
# small set of Postgres connections across many callers, which matters because
# Postgres allows few concurrent connections and serverless functions would
# otherwise open one each.
DATABASE_URL=""

# Direct (unpooled) connection, used by the Prisma CLI for migrations and
# introspection. DDL depends on session state a pooler may not preserve.
DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED=""

# Which Neon branch this checkout points at. Written by `neon checkout`.
NEON_BRANCH=""

# Optional: email for the idempotent curator seed (`npx prisma db seed`).
# SEED_CURATOR_EMAIL="you@example.com"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Added in later phases — see docs/ROADMAP.md
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 3, authentication (Auth.js + Google OAuth)
# AUTH_SECRET=""
# AUTH_GOOGLE_ID=""
# AUTH_GOOGLE_SECRET=""

# Phase 4, AI-assisted exercise entry (Gemini). Server-side only.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=""
